---
import '../styles/glhc003.css';
import config from '../../public/site-config.js?raw';
const registrationUrl = config.match(/lumaUrl:\s*'([^']+)'/)?.[1];
if (!registrationUrl || !registrationUrl.startsWith('https://luma.com/')) throw new Error('A valid organizer Luma destination is required.');
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" class="static-motion">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#062f42" />
    <script is:inline>
      // Select layout before body parsing so native scroll restoration sees
      // the final chapter heights; no-JavaScript readers retain the static layout.
      if (!matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) {
        document.documentElement.classList.remove('static-motion');
      }
    </script>
    <meta name="description" content="Make waves with real Great Lakes data. A student hackathon for every skill level, with equipment provided and a $500 prize for the winning team." />
    <title>Great Lakes Hackathon Challenge</title>
    <link rel="preload" href="/assets/team-lab.webp" as="image" fetchpriority="high" />
    <link rel="preload" href="/fonts/google-sans/google-sans-latin.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin />
    <script is:inline src="/site-config.js"></script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#challenge">Skip to the challenge</a>
    <header class="site-header">
      <nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a class="button header-register" data-register href={registrationUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Register Now <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span><span class="sr-only"> on Luma (new tab)</span></a></nav>
    </header>
    <div id="stage" class="lake-stage" aria-hidden="true"><div class="lake-backdrop"></div><canvas id="buoy-canvas"></canvas><div class="fallback-illustration"><img src="/assets/buoy-cutout.webp" alt="" width="172" height="344" /></div><span id="stage-label" hidden>Surface view</span><output id="scene-readout" hidden data-progress="0" data-phase="surface" data-camera-parked="false" data-draw-calls="0" data-triangles="0" data-frame-ms="0"><span id="readout-progress"></span><span id="readout-phase"></span><span id="readout-render"></span></output></div>
    <div id="scene-loading" class="scene-loading" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden><span id="loading-label">Preparing the lake…</span><button id="scene-retry" type="button" hidden>Retry 3D</button></div>
    <main id="story">
      <section class="invitation chapter" id="invitation" aria-labelledby="invitation-title">
        <div class="hero-copy"><h1 id="invitation-title">Great Lakes<br />Hackathon <em>Challenge</em></h1></div>
        <figure class="hero-photo"><div class="hero-photo__frame"><img src="/assets/team-lab.webp" width="1276" height="960" alt="A group of students and researchers gathered around scientific equipment in a research laboratory." fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" /><span class="prize-burst"><span><strong>$500</strong>Prize</span></span></div><figcaption class="sr-only">A $500 prize for the winning team.</figcaption></figure>
        <p class="hero-description">Join solo or as a team and bring Great Lakes data to life through lights, sound, interactive dashboards, or something entirely new. We want to see your ideas!</p>
        <nav class="hero-actions" aria-label="Explore the event"><a class="button hero-jump" href="#surface">What’s this about?</a><a class="button hero-jump" href="#how-it-works">What’s the challenge?</a></nav>
        <a class="scroll-cue" href="#surface">SCROLL FOR A COOL BREAKDOWN<img src="/assets/scroll_down.svg" alt="" width="48" height="48" aria-hidden="true" /><span class="scroll-cue-static" aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
      </section>
      <section class="surface chapter" id="surface" aria-labelledby="surface-title" tabindex="-1">
        <div class="surface-copy editorial-copy"><p class="eyebrow">01 / AT THE SURFACE</p><h2 id="surface-title">A lake full<br />of questions.</h2><p>Across the Great Lakes, scientists and researchers deploy monitoring equipment to observe how the water is changing.</p></div>
        <figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/team-water.webp" alt="Researchers wearing flotation suits aboard a boat with scientific monitoring equipment." width="712" height="950" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption>Research begins with people, equipment, and a question.</figcaption></figure>
        <p class="surface-note">Follow the buoy beneath the surface <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></p>
        <div class="static-buoy"><img src="/assets/buoy-reference.webp" alt="Yellow monitoring buoy with a solar-panel tower and instruments for collecting lake observations." width="600" height="600" loading="lazy" /></div>
      </section>
      <section class="crossing chapter" id="crossing" aria-labelledby="crossing-title"><div class="crossing-copy"><p class="eyebrow">02 / BENEATH THE SURFACE</p><h2 id="crossing-title">A different<br />perspective.</h2><p>Below the float, scientific instruments help turn the lake’s changing conditions into observations.</p></div></section>
      <section class="science chapter" id="science" aria-label="Understanding the science">
        <div class="science-copy"><div class="science-copy__inner"><p class="eyebrow">03 / UNDERSTANDING THE SCIENCE</p><div class="panel-window" id="panel-window"><div class="panel-track" id="panel-track">
          <article class="science-panel" id="panel-one"><h2>Signals from<br />the lake.</h2><p>Buoys equipped with scientific sensors collect measurements such as water temperature, dissolved oxygen, and indicators of algal activity. These observations help researchers understand how conditions in the Great Lakes change over time.</p></article>
          <article class="science-panel" id="panel-two"><h2>A shared<br />freshwater future.</h2><p>The Great Lakes support millions of people, provide drinking water, and sustain important ecosystems. Pollution, warming temperatures, and harmful algal blooms can threaten their health. Understanding these changes helps scientists and communities make informed decisions.</p></article>
        </div></div><p class="science-cue" aria-hidden="true">Keep scrolling to follow the story <span>↓</span></p></div></div>
      </section>
      <section class="challenge chapter" id="challenge" aria-labelledby="challenge-title">
        <div class="challenge-intro editorial-copy"><p class="eyebrow">04 / YOUR CHALLENGE</p><h2 id="challenge-title">Make the data<br /><em>mean something.</em></h2><p>Use real Great Lakes water-quality data and open hardware to create something that helps people connect with the lakes.</p><p>Water-quality data doesn’t have to live on a spreadsheet. It can become something people see, experience, and connect with.</p></div>
        <figure class="collage"><h3>There’s inspiration<br />to draw from.</h3><img src="/assets/glhc-communication-collage-640.webp" srcset="/assets/glhc-communication-collage-640.webp 640w, /assets/glhc-communication-collage-1080.webp 1080w" sizes="(min-width: 900px) 48vw, 90vw" width="1080" height="1080" alt="Collage of a green illuminated waterfront installation, an electronics controller with lights, and a purple LED display." loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption>Light. Hardware. A new way of seeing.<span>Illustrative inspiration for what data can become.</span></figcaption></figure>
      </section>
      <section class="how-it-works chapter" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="how-title" tabindex="-1">
        <div class="how-intro"><p class="eyebrow">CURIOSITY IS YOUR STARTING POINT</p><h2 id="how-title">You bring the idea.<br /><em>We’ll bring the tools.</em></h2><p>You don’t have to arrive knowing how to build it. Bring your perspective, learn together, and see where it leads.</p></div>
        <ol class="participation"><li><span class="step" aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><h3>Work in teams.</h3><p>Form or join a team and collaborate with other students.</p></div></li><li><span class="step" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><h3>Use real Great Lakes data.</h3><p>Work with scientific water-quality measurements collected through research partnerships.</p></div></li><li><span class="step" aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><h3>Use provided equipment.</h3><p>Open hardware tools and equipment help bring your ideas to life.</p></div></li><li><span class="step" aria-hidden="true">04</span><div><h3>All skill levels welcome.</h3><p>No previous coding, electronics, design, or hackathon experience required.</p></div></li><li><span class="step" aria-hidden="true">05</span><div><h3>Create for public audiences.</h3><p>Build something engaging that helps others connect with Great Lakes water-quality information.</p></div></li></ol>
      </section>
      <section class="registration chapter" id="registration" aria-labelledby="registration-title"><div class="registration-inner"><p class="eyebrow">05 / TAKE THE PLUNGE</p><h2 id="registration-title">Your idea could<br />make <em>waves.</em></h2><p class="registration-intro">No experience required. Bring your curiosity, work with a team, and create something worth sharing.</p><p class="registration-prize"><strong>$500</strong> for the winning team.</p><p>All experience levels welcome.<br />Your project could be showcased in public displays.</p><a class="button button--large" data-register href={registrationUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Register Now <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span><span class="sr-only"> on Luma (new tab)</span></a><p class="luma-note">Find current event details on Luma.<br />Registration opens in a new tab.</p></div></section>
    </main>
    <footer class="site-footer"><a href="#invitation">Great Lakes Hackathon Challenge</a><span>Real data. Shared curiosity. New possibilities.</span><label class="motion-toggle"><input id="reduce-motion" type="checkbox" /><span>Less motion</span></label><a href="#invitation">Back to the surface ↑</a></footer>
    <script>import '../scripts/glhc003/bootstrap.js';</script>
  </body>
</html>
